    "created_at": "2018-03-15T11:01:45Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-03-15T11:01:45Z",
    "body": "It seems that similar to https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsing-the-web.html#unloading-document-cleanup-steps looping over `EventSource` objects, we should have \"close a worker\" do the same.\r\n\r\nFurthermore, we'll need to make \"terminate a worker\" invoke \"close a worker\" to avoid duplicating its first two steps and this new step.\r\n\r\n(It's a little bit unclear to me if the last step of \"terminate a worker\" should also be present in \"close a worker\". It kinda seems like it should be.)",
